  "note": "Mathlib's mellin f s = ∫ t in Ioi 0, t^(s−1) • f t has the book's normalization (dt/t, t^s). Lean never defines F_δ for the plain Gaussian e^{−t²/2}; it works with G_δ = F_δ(·+2) and with mellin (fP δ)."
